thank you  Brothers in Arms Gianluca viali  embracing Roberto Mancini his former  teammate and friend for over 40 years  after watching Italy win the Euros in  2021  Mancini the head coach had hired the Ali  as the team's delegation Chief a role he  continued in until last month before  stepping away to focus on his health  viali was originally diagnosed with  pancreatic cancer in 2017 but given the  all clear a year later only for it to  return a few months after Italy's  Triumph at Wembley Stadium he died on  Friday leaving his wife and two  daughters  it's a sad day for me I say goodbye to a  friend a colleague a very nice person a  great player may he rest in peace  the Ali's career took off when he signed  for sampdoria in 1984. he scored 85  League goals won the serial title three  Italian cups and the European Cup  winners cup as well  he was soon called up to the national  team and went on to play 59 times for  Italy representing them at two World  Cups Mexico 1986 an Italia 90.  in 1992 we secured a then world record  move to Juventus for 15 million dollars  he won another Italian title the UEFA  Cup and the prestigious Champions League  Juventus coach massimiliano allegri led  a minute silence at his press conference  on Friday before paying his own tribute  representative he represented a lot  firstly as a player but even more as a  man I think that for the younger players  he was a model to follow therefore we  will all miss him terribly after  Juventus fiali's next move was to the  Premier League when rude hullit brought  him in at Chelsea he ended up replacing  the Dutchman as player manager and  guided the London side to five trophies  and there it is his first goal in a  Chelsea shirt this was somebody who  introduced us to a new era of quality at  the club whose ability to communicate  the link between the players and the  supporters  um was absolutely everything to us  a minute silence will be held across all  Seria matches this weekend in memory of  viali Italy's Football Federation  president said his sporting success was  matched by his extraordinary human  qualities

